+10. publishes the meta package when requested
+
+## Linux Runtime Compatibility Gate
+
+The npm workflow must catch runtime linker failures before `npm publish`.
+
+After staging platform packages, it creates local tarballs for:
+
+- `ai-wiki-toolkit-linux-x64`
+- `ai-wiki-toolkit`
+
+It then installs those tarballs in a clean `node:24-bookworm` linux/amd64 container and runs:
+
+```bash
+aiwiki-toolkit --version
+```
+
+This mirrors the user-facing npm wrapper path closely enough to catch Python shared library and GLIBC compatibility failures in the Linux binary package before any npm package is published.
 
 Before enabling `NPM_PUBLISH_ENABLED`, make sure the npm platform target map only advertises targets that the `Release Binaries` workflow actually publishes.
 
